From: sanders-linux-mainline port
Date: 2026-06-06
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8953: fix wcnss reserved memory range

The WCNSS/Pronto firmware ELF (wcnss.mdt) loads its first PT_LOAD segment
at physical address 0x8e600000, but the reserved memory region was defined
starting at 0x8e700000 — 1MB too high.

qcom_mdt_load() validates that every PT_LOAD segment falls within the
reserved region:

  if (phdr->p_paddr < mem_phys)
      return -EINVAL;

This caused qcom-wcnss-pil to fail unconditionally with -22 (EINVAL) on
any wcnss firmware, regardless of the actual firmware content.

Firmware load range (from wcnss.mdt program headers):
  First segment: 0x8e600000
  Last segment:  0x8ec56128  (total ~6.3 MB, fits within 7 MB region)

Fix: move the WCNSS reserved region base from 0x8e700000 to 0x8e600000,
keeping the same 7 MB size (0x700000). Shorten the adjacent ADSP reserved
region by 1 MB so it ends at 0x8e600000 and does not overlap WCNSS.

Signed-off-by: sanders-linux-mainline port
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi
index 753167c3f..97de4fb56 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953.dtsi
@@ -314,4 +314,4 @@ mpss_mem: mpss@86c00000 {
 		adsp_fw_mem: adsp@8d600000 {
-			reg = <0x0 0x8d600000 0x0 0x1100000>;
+			reg = <0x0 0x8d600000 0x0 0x1000000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
@@ -319,4 +319,4 @@ mpss_mem: mpss@86c00000 {
-		wcnss_fw_mem: wcnss@8e700000 {
-			reg = <0x0 0x8e700000 0x0 0x700000>;
+		wcnss_fw_mem: wcnss@8e600000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x8e600000 0x0 0x700000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
